id: TASK_026_V002
title: Replace hardcoded temp password with random password generation for approved registration users
status: REJECTED
priority: high
depends_on: []

rejection_reason: >
  Task is incomplete with critical safety gap. The task requires generating random passwords
  but does not specify how to deliver them to users. The notes warn about email service
  dependency, but the task should be blocked until email infrastructure exists and is verified.
  Executing this task without email service would permanently lock users out of their accounts.

required_fixes:
  - Add pre-condition check for email service availability before password generation
  - Add alternative secure password delivery mechanism (e.g., temporary admin-settable password)
  - Add retry logic for email delivery failures
  - Consider forced password change on first login
  - Specify exact error handling for email delivery failures

original_description: >
  The admin approval endpoint creates users with a predictable hardcoded password "temppass123".
  No email notification is sent. This is a security risk.

goals:
  - Generate a random secure password for approved registration users
  - Send the password via email to the user
  - Force password change on first login (optional, if time permits)

files:
  - path: src/mkobi/api/routes/admin.py
    targets:
      - type: function
        name: approve_registration_request_admin_endpoint

notes: >
  REJECTED: Requires email infrastructure verification before execution.
  See rejection_reason for required fixes.